   "stick": "toward"
  },
  "reap": {
   "ground": true
  },
  "breach": {
   "fighters": [
    "protagonist"
   ]
  }
 },
 "patternRule": "every blur string draws one open pattern, with its cadence, at its first blow (patternGates). Each light of the string takes the next step, filled from the fighter's blur lights with that limb and target (pieces), no key strike twice in a string; a string that runs past the fifth step starts the pattern again. The pattern's own closing blow is drawn from the ender pool and lands where the string's last light landed, when a piece of that pool does; otherwise any piece of it. A pattern carries no ticks: the gap between blows is the string's cadence, the director's number",
 "beat": {
  "_about": "The beat point of a light or a skill strike: ticks after its contact at which the next press is on the beat (Game Design: 24 by default, 20 to 28 by the piece). By the piece's path. default serves a piece with no path",
  "line": 20,
  "arc_in": 24,
  "arc_out": 24,
  "rise": 24,
  "drop": 26,
  "spin": 28,
  "default": 24
 },
 "brawl": {
  "_about": "Which pool each kind of press in the martial arts stance draws on (docs/design/melee-press-feel.md sections 3 to 5 and 13). The first three and the ender name pools that are live today. flurry and skill split the lights: a missed beat lapses from the skill pool to the flurry pool. lift, break and ender are the three things a heavy can be. When the filters (a broken limb, the ground, a repeat) leave one of the five new pools empty, the draw falls back to light for flurry, skill and juggle, and to heavy for lift and break",
  "light": "combo.link",
  "lightToward": "blur.toward",
  "heavy": "power",
  "ender": "power.last",
  "flurry": "brawl.flurry",
  "skill": "brawl.skill",
  "juggle": "brawl.skill",
  "lift": "brawl.lift",
  "break": "brawl.break"
 },
